// Single source of truth for the AzureVisionLiveness sample backend host.
// Referenced from:
//   - FaceAnalyzerSample/FaceAnalyzerSample.entitlements        (applinks:$(LIVENESS_HOST))
//   - FaceAnalyzerSampleAppClip/FaceAnalyzerSampleAppClip.entitlements (appclips:/applinks:$(LIVENESS_HOST))
//   - FaceAnalyzerSample/Info.plist and FaceAnalyzerSampleAppClip/Info.plist (LivenessHost = $(LIVENESS_HOST))
//   - FaceAnalyzerSample/UniversalLinkProcessor.swift reads LivenessHost from Bundle at runtime.
//
// Replace `example.com` below with the host of the liveness backend you operate
// before building. The "Verify LIVENESS_HOST" build phase will fail the build
// if this is left as the example.com placeholder.
//
// This single value drives local single-domain builds. To associate the apps
// with ONE or MULTIPLE backend domains, run scripts/apply-liveness-hosts.sh with
// your host list (see scripts/README.md). That script — which lives with this
// sample, not the CI pipeline — sets LIVENESS_HOST below to the primary (first)
// host and expands the full list into the associated-domains entitlements + the
// LivenessHosts Info.plist whitelist (read at runtime by allowedLivenessHosts()).
// The CI pipeline invokes the same script.
LIVENESS_HOST = example.com
